INT. HOTEL BALLROOM - 24-HOUR TABLE TENNIS MARATHON - NIGHT

Chandeliers dimmed to amber. One green table in the center of a vast parquet floor. Folding chairs along the walls, empty. A banner sagging between two columns: HOUR 19.

NORIKO ABE, 40s, in a faded tracksuit with a sweatband, bounces the ball once off her paddle. DESMOND CRAWLEY, 50s, in bright orange shorts, stands across from her, red-faced, shoulders heaving.

The scoreboard reads 10-10. A cardboard sign propped against it: SUDDEN DEATH.

DESMOND
(to the empty ballroom)
Did everyone hear that? Ten-all!

Nobody answers. A janitor's vacuum hums far away.

NORIKO
Serve.

DESMOND
I know it's my serve.

NORIKO
Then serve.

DESMOND
I'm gathering my thoughts.

NORIKO
They've scattered.

Desmond tosses the ball. Whacks it. It flies in a slow arc. Noriko returns, short, with a flick of the wrist. Desmond lunges, snaps a backhand over the net. Noriko leaps, smashes, and the ball cracks onto the table and into the dark, and Desmond, chasing it, goes down hard against a stack of chairs, which clatter across the floor like dropped cutlery while Noriko, arms raised, is already celebrating alone.

NORIKO (CONT'D)
Point!

Desmond sits up. Chairs are tangled around his legs.

DESMOND
Out!

NORIKO
It was on the line.

DESMOND
It was off the line.

NORIKO
It kissed the line.

DESMOND
(muttering)
It kissed my dignity.

He gets to his feet. Pulls a chair off his shin. Looks at the scoreboard. 11-10.

DESMOND (CONT'D)
(to the room)
For the record, I'd like it noted that I was provoked.

NORIKO
By what?

DESMOND
By you existing.

She smiles. It is the first smile of the night.

NORIKO
Match point.

DESMOND
Don't.

NORIKO
Your serve.

DESMOND
(grim)
Fine.

He retrieves the ball from beneath a chair. Wipes it on his shorts. Steps to the end of the table. Stares at her, then at the ball, then at the chandelier.

DESMOND (CONT'D)
(to himself)
Twenty-four hours. One ball. Two idiots.

He serves. A looping, impossible spin. Noriko tracks it. Lifts her paddle. Misses by an inch.

The ball bounces off the table. Drifts across the ballroom. Rolls to a stop at a vacuum cleaner's wheels.

A long silence. They both stare at it.

NORIKO
Eleven-eleven.

DESMOND
It's a point for me!

NORIKO
It's a point for you.

DESMOND
It's eleven-eleven.

NORIKO
You need two.

DESMOND
I know that!

He walks down the room to fetch the ball. His shoes squeak on the parquet. Behind him, Noriko sinks onto the edge of the table, rubs her wrist, and looks at the banner. HOUR 19. She counts silently on her fingers.

NORIKO
(under her breath)
Five more hours.

Desmond returns with the ball. He holds it up like a trophy.

DESMOND
Found it.

NORIKO
It didn't go far.

DESMOND
Nothing in this room goes far.

They look at each other. Both, slowly, start to laugh. Neither can stop. Desmond has to put the paddle down. Noriko wipes her eyes.

NORIKO
Why are we here?

DESMOND
For charity.

NORIKO
Which one?

DESMOND
I don't remember.

NORIKO
Serve, Desmond.

DESMOND
(winded, grinning)
Serving.

He serves. She returns. They rally. It goes on and on, ball ticking over the net, the sound filling the ballroom like the beating of a patient heart, until neither of them is keeping score.
